# One trailer closes more than one open level (the author 2026-11-11, LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#one-level-needs-no-close):
# `end: Other` at the level of Other closes Other across the open Point, and the construction admits it.
# Plan M11 5v: the named Structures live in the data part of main (ROOT5V); the root holds the places and the call main().
# Observation: an explicit write through a path in main (#flush-receiver-contract, #call-frame-20261115).
(
    Observed:
        int: after 0
        int: x 0
)
@: shared data[0]
sub: main () (
    Other:
        Point:
            int: x 4
    end: Other
)
    int: after 1
    shared\Observed\after := after
    shared\Observed\x := Other\Point\x
main()
